<h2>Percentage deductibles in plain numbers</h2>
<p>A 2% hurricane deductible on a home insured for $525,000 is $10,500 — ten times a typical $1,000 flat deductible. On beach homes in Rehoboth, Bethany or Fenwick with higher dwelling limits, the dollar figure climbs quickly.</p>
<h2>When does the hurricane deductible apply?</h2>
<p>That depends entirely on your policy’s definition. Some apply when the National Weather Service names a storm or issues a hurricane watch or warning for any part of the state, and remain in effect for a set period afterward. Others apply only to damage from a hurricane itself. A tornado or nor’easter may fall under the regular deductible. Read your endorsement carefully.</p>
<h2>Why it matters for disputes</h2>
<p>When a large deductible applies, every dollar of under-scoped damage comes straight out of your pocket. A thorough estimate is the only way to recover the amount above the deductible that you’re actually owed.</p>
<h2>Questions about this worksheet</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is the deductible based on the loss or the coverage amount?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Percentage deductibles are usually calculated on the Coverage A (dwelling) limit, not the size of the loss.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I lower my hurricane deductible?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Sometimes, at renewal, for a higher premium. Talk with your agent; it can’t be changed after a loss.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does the hurricane deductible apply to nor’easters?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Usually not, unless the policy definition is broad enough to include them. Check the wording.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free worksheets</h2><div class="cards cards-3"><a class="card card-tool rv" href="/claim-worksheets/policy-deadline-calendar/"><span class="card-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/inspector-clipboard.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/inspector-clipboard-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/inspector-clipboard.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="960" height="640" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="card-tag">Planner</span></span><span class="card-body"><h3 class="card-t">Claim Deadline Calendar</h3><span class="card-p">Map notice, 